A timing belt has both a mileage limit and a time limit. The correct interval depends on your engine, so check the vehicle handbook or ask your garage.

## Start with the service history

Find the date and mileage of the last replacement. If the history is unknown, ask a garage to assess what needs doing rather than assuming the belt is recent.

## Set your own reminder

In Revly you can record maintenance and set reminders based on time or mileage. Use the interval for your car, rather than a generic number from the internet.

[See how maintenance records work](/en/onderhoud/).
